    },
    {
      "mechanism": "Cost Amortization",
      "description": "Verification of zero-knowledge proofs on-chain is computationally expensive and gas-heavy. SNARKtor amortizes the on-chain verification gas cost across hundreds or thousands of transactions, lowering end-user fees on Telos and connected rollups."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "Decentralized Aggregation Network",
      "description": "Unlike centralized proof routers, SNARKtor operates as a decentralized network of aggregators. This prevents single-point-of-failure censorship, maintains liveness, and distributes the computational workload of recursive proof composition."
